Add a kernel.org Edge mirror as a fallback for linux tarball downloads.

The default CT_Mirrors function returns only cdn.kernel.org for
kernel.org/linux. When that single CDN endpoint hiccups (observed as a
transient "linux: download failed" while pulling linux-5.4.296 from a
US Azure runner), CT_GetFile has nothing else to try and the whole
build aborts. Adding the kernel.org Edge mirror as a second URL lets
CT_GetFile fall back to a distinct infrastructure path (kernel.org's
official Edge mirror network, separate from the Fastly-fronted cdn
endpoint) before failing.

diff --git a/scripts/functions b/scripts/functions
--- a/scripts/functions
+++ b/scripts/functions
@@ -1811,7 +1811,8 @@
                 # Ignore, this happens before .config is fully evaluated
                 ;;
             [3456].*)
                 echo "https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v${version%%.*}.x"
+                echo "https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v${version%%.*}.x"
                 ;;
             2.6.*)
                 echo "https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v2.6"
